.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAP-LIST-EGRESS-SITES 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eap-list-egress-sites \- list the outside sites applications call through egress permits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eap list-egress-sites
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists every outside site an application has asked an egress permit for,
or that has a limit set, with the limits it's held to and how it stands
now. See
.BR euclid-cli-eap-set-egress-limit (1)
for what egress permits are. The caller must be an administrator.
.PP
The JSON response has
.I defaultLimits
(from
.IR euclid.modules.eap.egress.default )
and a
.I sites
array, sorted by site, each with:
.RS
.TP
.I site
The host name.
.TP
.I limits
.IR requestsPerSecond ", " burst " and " concurrent
in force for it.
.TP
.I limitsSet
.I true
if they were set with
.BR set-egress-limit ;
.I false
if they're the default.
.TP
.I tokens
Requests that could start right now as far as the rate goes - up to the
burst.
.TP
.I inFlight
Permits held: requests to the site that have started and not finished.
Includes those of an instance that died, until their lease runs out.
.TP
.I blockedUntil
When the site asked to be left alone (a 429 or 503 an application
reported) and nothing is granted until then; empty if it isn't blocked.
.TP
.I lastUsed
When anybody last asked for, or gave back, a permit for it.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eap list-egress-sites
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-set-egress-limit (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-delete-egress-limit (1)
